        "original_id": "ce630504-ce2c-5a5c-b6e1-5cd0cf844c58",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Northwest Territories, Canada; Yellowknife\n- Companies: Tundra Mines; Negus Mine; Salmita Mine\n- Topics: Gold mining; ore processing infrastructure\n\nFacts:\n- Negus Mine was a gold producer at Yellowknife in the Northwest Territories, Canada, from 1939 to 1952.\n- Tundra Mines was a gold producer in the Northwest Territories, Canada, from 1964 to 1968.\n- Tundra Mines produced 104,476 troy ounces of gold from 187,714 tons of ore.\n- Salmita Mine used the old camp and milling plant of the abandoned Tundra Mine, which was located a few kilometres to the south.",
